DOCUMENT
TITLE: Software Architecture Requirements
UID: REQ-ARCH-001
VERSION: 1.0
CLASSIFICATION: Internal
REQ_TYPE: System Requirements

CONTENT
{FREE_TEXT}
This document defines the software architecture requirements for a modern web application system. The architecture must support scalability, maintainability, and security while providing excellent user experience.

The system shall be designed following microservices principles with clear separation of concerns and well-defined interfaces between components.
{FREE_TEXT}

[SECTION]
TITLE: System Overview
UID: REQ-ARCH-002
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: architecture, overview, system-design
TITLE: System Architecture Overview
STATEMENT: The system shall implement a three-tier architecture consisting of presentation layer, business logic layer, and data access layer.
RATIONALE: Three-tier architecture provides clear separation of concerns, enables independent scaling of layers, and facilitates maintenance and testing.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Presentation Layer Requirements
UID: REQ-ARCH-003
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: frontend, ui, presentation
TITLE: Frontend Architecture Requirements
STATEMENT: The presentation layer shall be built using modern web technologies including React.js for component-based UI development.
RATIONALE: React.js provides excellent developer experience, large ecosystem, and proven scalability for complex user interfaces.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-004
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: responsive, mobile, accessibility
TITLE: Responsive Design Requirement
STATEMENT: The user interface shall be responsive and support multiple screen sizes from mobile devices to desktop computers.
RATIONALE: Users access applications from various devices, and responsive design ensures consistent user experience across all platforms.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-005
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: accessibility, wcag, compliance
TITLE: Accessibility Compliance
STATEMENT: The user interface shall comply with WCAG 2.1 AA standards for accessibility.
RATIONALE: Accessibility compliance ensures the application is usable by people with disabilities and may be legally required in many jurisdictions.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Business Logic Layer Requirements
UID: REQ-ARCH-006
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: backend, api, microservices
TITLE: Backend Architecture Requirements
STATEMENT: The business logic shall be implemented as microservices using RESTful APIs with JSON data exchange.
RATIONALE: Microservices architecture enables independent development, deployment, and scaling of different system components.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-007
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: authentication, security, oauth
TITLE: Authentication and Authorization
STATEMENT: The system shall implement OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect for user authentication and role-based access control.
RATIONALE: OAuth 2.0 is the industry standard for secure authentication and provides flexibility for different client types.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-008
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: caching, performance, redis
TITLE: Caching Strategy
STATEMENT: The system shall implement Redis for session management and application-level caching to improve performance.
RATIONALE: Caching reduces database load and improves response times for frequently accessed data.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Data Layer Requirements
UID: REQ-ARCH-009
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: database, persistence, data
TITLE: Data Persistence Requirements
STATEMENT: The system shall use PostgreSQL as the primary database with read replicas for scalability.
RATIONALE: PostgreSQL provides ACID compliance, excellent performance, and robust features for complex data operations.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-010
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: backup, disaster-recovery, data-protection
TITLE: Data Backup and Recovery
STATEMENT: The system shall implement automated daily backups with point-in-time recovery capability.
RATIONALE: Regular backups protect against data loss and enable recovery from various failure scenarios.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-011
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: encryption, security, data-protection
TITLE: Data Encryption
STATEMENT: All sensitive data shall be encrypted at rest using AES-256 encryption.
RATIONALE: Data encryption protects sensitive information from unauthorized access and meets regulatory compliance requirements.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Integration Requirements
UID: REQ-ARCH-012
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: integration, messaging, event-driven
TITLE: Service Integration
STATEMENT: Services shall communicate using asynchronous messaging with Apache Kafka for event-driven architecture.
RATIONALE: Event-driven architecture enables loose coupling between services and supports high-throughput data processing.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-013
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: monitoring, observability, logging
TITLE: Monitoring and Observability
STATEMENT: The system shall implement comprehensive logging, metrics collection, and distributed tracing using ELK stack.
RATIONALE: Monitoring and observability are essential for detecting issues, performance optimization, and operational excellence.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-014
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: api-gateway, routing, load-balancing
TITLE: API Gateway
STATEMENT: The system shall use an API gateway for request routing, load balancing, and rate limiting.
RATIONALE: API gateway provides centralized control over API access, security, and traffic management.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Deployment Requirements
UID: REQ-ARCH-015
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: deployment, containerization, orchestration
TITLE: Containerization and Orchestration
STATEMENT: The system shall be containerized using Docker and orchestrated with Kubernetes for automated deployment and scaling.
RATIONALE: Containerization ensures consistent deployment across environments, while Kubernetes provides robust orchestration capabilities.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-016
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: ci-cd, automation, deployment
TITLE: Continuous Integration and Deployment
STATEMENT: The system shall implement CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions for automated testing and deployment.
RATIONALE: CI/CD automation reduces manual errors, accelerates delivery, and ensures consistent quality across deployments.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-017
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: infrastructure, cloud, scalability
TITLE: Cloud Infrastructure
STATEMENT: The system shall be deployed on AWS cloud infrastructure with auto-scaling capabilities.
RATIONALE: Cloud infrastructure provides flexibility, scalability, and cost-effectiveness for modern applications.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Security Requirements
UID: REQ-ARCH-018
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: security, compliance, audit
TITLE: Security Framework
STATEMENT: The system shall implement security controls based on OWASP Top 10 and NIST Cybersecurity Framework.
RATIONALE: Following established security frameworks ensures comprehensive protection against common vulnerabilities and threats.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-019
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: ssl, tls, encryption
TITLE: Transport Security
STATEMENT: All external communications shall use TLS 1.3 encryption for data in transit.
RATIONALE: TLS encryption protects data during transmission and is essential for maintaining data confidentiality and integrity.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-ARCH-020
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: audit, compliance, logging
TITLE: Security Auditing
STATEMENT: The system shall maintain comprehensive audit logs for all security-relevant events and user actions.
RATIONALE: Audit logs are essential for security monitoring, incident response, and compliance with regulatory requirements. 